  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Wear Black** (1 review): The intro banter to this song showcases John's rapport with the audience [4]\n- **Unicorn Tolerance** (1 review): John's connection with the crowd shows in the banter introducing this song [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Xolo**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Love Cuts The Strings**: back after 28 archived shows (735 days) [5]\n- **Paid in Cocaine**: rare: 10 archived performances [5]\n- **Song For My Sons (Sarah Groves Cover)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **International Small Arms Traffic Blues**: back after 44 archived shows (1427 days) [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2017-06-02** (recommended): source not stated; 28 songs; 147 min; rated 4.67/5 by 3 [1]. Said about its sound: Balcony recording is strong; the nearby recorder didn't pick up much of the reviewer's loud singing; Described as a lovely recording that preserves a fond memory of the night [2][3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: (John fell over while rocking out, is indestructible) International Small Arms, Applause Break.. San Bernardino, No Children, Praise Jordan..General [1]\n- By the end of the night John was very drunk and slurring some lyrics [2]\n- Reviewer was at their first Mountain Goats concert, attending from San Jose, and sang along loudly during the taping [3]\n- John's voice was worn by the end; Matt Douglas's saxophone playing stood out [4]\n- Hearing the new Goths tracks live won the reviewer over after being lukewarm on the album [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2017-06-02**: taped by LMGBTapes; transferred by LMGBTapes; source: Zoom H4n Pro Onboard Mics [1]",
